Wings patch 0013: hard token and spend caps for agent runs

Upstream caps an agent run by rounds and tool calls only; it tracks
tokens and estimated cost for display but nothing stops on them.
OpenManus can stop on a token count (input tokens only, off by default).
Wings counts input and output tokens and estimated dollars, per run and
per person per day, including scheduled tasks; see wings/budget.py.

  * src/agent_loop.py: the run's usage_buckets list is a wings RunUsage,
    which counts each round as upstream records it (all four sites). A
    person whose daily cap is used up gets a message instead of a run.
    Before any tool of a round runs, a run or daily cap that is reached
    stops the run through upstream's budget_exceeded path.
  * routes/chat_helpers.py: _enforce_chat_privileges refuses a new chat
    or agent message with 429 when the daily cap is used up (admins
    included); accumulate_token_usage counts plain chat turns.
  * static/js/chat.js: budget_exceeded shows the message it carries.

All caps are off unless set in .env (WINGS_RUN_MAX_TOKENS,
WINGS_RUN_MAX_USD, WINGS_DAY_MAX_TOKENS, WINGS_DAY_MAX_USD).

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

diff --git a/routes/chat_helpers.py b/routes/chat_helpers.py
index eb0bfc3..0eb45bf 100644
--- a/routes/chat_helpers.py
+++ b/routes/chat_helpers.py
@@ -485,6 +485,12 @@ def _enforce_chat_privileges(request, sess) -> None:
         user = effective_user(request)
     except Exception:
         user = None
+    # Wings: daily token and spend caps apply to everyone, admins included
+    # (wings/budget.py; off unless set in .env).
+    from wings import budget as _wings_budget
+    _wings_stop = _wings_budget.day_exhausted(user or None)
+    if _wings_stop:
+        raise HTTPException(429, _wings_stop)
     if not user:
         return
     auth_manager = getattr(getattr(request.app, "state", None), "auth_manager", None)
@@ -1299,6 +1305,10 @@ async def build_chat_context(
 
 def accumulate_token_usage(session_id: str, metrics: dict):
     """Add input/output token counts (and USD cost) to the session's totals."""
+    # Wings: plain chat turns count toward the daily caps (agent runs are
+    # counted round by round in the agent loop).
+    from wings import budget as _wings_budget
+    _wings_budget.record_chat_turn(session_id, metrics)
     in_t = metrics.get("input_tokens", 0)
     out_t = metrics.get("output_tokens", 0)
     cost = metrics.get("cost_usd")
